    {
      "args": {
        "blockId": "S2"
      },
      "command": "get_properties",
      "comment": "`get_properties_inner` reads `block_properties` and nothing else, so the reserved key `todo_state` — which the projection routes to the block's own COLUMN — must be ABSENT here even though the op that set it looks identical to the others. The deleted `temp` key must be absent too. The remaining four pin the typed-value projection, including the `Ref` whose value is relabeled to a canonical token.",
      "name": "get_properties_excludes_column_routed_key"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "blockId": "S2",
        "key": "flag"
      },
      "command": "get_property",
      "comment": "`flag` is stored `false` (SQLite `0`). A hit must project as a ROW, not as a miss — the classic reimplementation bug is a truthiness test on the value that collapses a present-but-falsy property into `null`. Paired with the next step, this is the present-vs-absent distinction.",
      "name": "get_property_present_but_falsy"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "blockId": "S2",
        "key": "temp"
      },
      "command": "get_property",
      "comment": "The other half of the pair: `temp` was set and then deleted, so the PK lookup misses and the command answers `None`. Empty on purpose — what it pins is that a deleted key is absent rather than present-with-a-null-value, which the previous step's non-empty result makes a real distinction instead of a vacuous one.",
      "expect_empty": true,
      "name": "get_property_absent_after_delete"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "blockIds": ["S2", "S3"]
      },
      "command": "get_batch_properties",
      "comment": "Both requested blocks own properties, so this pins the GROUPING: every key must land under its own block, and S3's `status` must not leak into S2's bucket (both blocks carry a key of that name with different values). The present-but-empty map entry is pinned separately in `query_batch_properties_empty_entry`.",
      "name": "get_batch_properties_groups_by_block"
    }
  ],
